    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Michael Boland is delighted to present this attractive two-bedroom single-storey cottage, ideally positioned in the highly sought-after Quay Village area of Ballina.\n\nThe property offers well-proportioned accommodation comprising two bedrooms, a bright living room, a separate lounge area, a kitchen /dining area and office space. While presented in good condition, the property would benefit from further modernisation and offers excellent potential for redevelopment. Its convenient single-storey layout will appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including families, downsizers, investors and those seeking a retirement home.\n\nA particularly appealing feature is the large mature garden to the rear. Beautifully established and offering generous outdoor space, it is a true gardener's paradise with excellent potential for further landscaping, outdoor entertaining or future development, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe property enjoys an enviable setting overlooking the River Moy Estuary towards the mature woodland of Belleek Woods, creating a wonderful backdrop and a strong sense of tranquillity while remaining within easy reach of Ballina town centre.\n\nThe cottage is within walking distance of Tom Ruane Park, the new Ballina Sensory Park, the renowned Ice House Hotel, local shops, restaurants, bars and Ballina Rugby Club. The Quay National School and secondary schools are also within walking distance, making this a particularly convenient location for families.\n\nAdding further appeal, an investment of over 7.5 million has recently been announced for the redevelopment and regeneration of the Ballina Quay area, which is set to further enhance the waterfront, public realm and overall attractiveness of this already popular location.\n\nFor those who enjoy the coast, the popular seaside resort of Enniscrone is approximately a ten-minute drive away, offering its renowned beach, golf course and range of leisure amenities.\n\nCombining a highly desirable Quay Village setting, two-bedroom single-storey accommodation, a large mature rear garden, attractive views across the River Moy Estuary towards Belleek Woods and excellent potential for modernisation or redevelopment, this property represents an exciting opportunity to create a truly special home in one of Ballina's most appealing residential areas.\n\nCall DNG Michael Boland today to arrange a viewing."
      },
